            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dianna Harkins Purvis"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Didn’t change anything, but did put fruit cocktail in. Allows more flavors. It’s made every holiday",
            "datePublished": "2024-06-23T17:31:05.617Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "E Devos"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We always called this stuff \"Ambrosia.\" It's always delicious, and the fruit to be used can vary based on taste. My mother used to make this with canned oranges and pineapple chunks and chopped walnuts at Christmastime. My Aunt used to throw in coconut and marshmallows. They called it salad, but we always thought it was a dessert. I'm going to try this version with the cherries, but I am going to use canned or frozen cherries instead of the pie filling.",
            "datePublished": "2025-05-20T21:19:26.548Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
